        // Let's simplify this function to only add classes and event listeners to the existing `ul`, `li`, `a` elements.

        // The original HTML shows `header-comp__wrapper--sub-menu-group` on the top-level UL inside the hierarchy-tree.
        // And `header-comp__wrapper--sub-menu-item child-below` on `li`s that have nested ULs.
        // And `header-comp__wrapper--menu-link dropdown-toggle` on the `div` that contains the `a` and toggles the submenu.

        // Let's modify `transformNestedLists` to apply classes and event listeners based on the original HTML's structure for nested menus.
        // The `hierarchyRoot` is the `ul` from the richtext.
        // The `transformNestedLists` function is called on `hierarchyRoot`.
        // The original HTML shows `ul class="header-comp__wrapper--sub-menu-group"` as the direct child of `header-comp__sub-menus` or `inner-childs`.
        // Inside this `ul`, there are `li`s.
        // If an `li` has a nested `ul`, it gets `child-below`.
        // The `div` that wraps the `a` inside the `li` gets `dropdown-toggle` and has the click handler.

        // This function is processing the *content* of the hierarchy-tree cell.
